{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right","id":966181,"title":"Ammon the Mage, Did I do this right?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mage: The Awakening"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-09-09T06:39:11-07:00","id":966181,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Ammon the Mage, Did I do this right?","content":"Below is my character Please help me make sure I built him correctly. For the game my character is supposed to be inspired by me, though is timeline and mine diverged almost a decade ago so our stats skills sets are going to be very different.<br /> <br /> As I have said in other threads but now I'm pulling everything together into one place Here is his back story. It plays off the ending of our last Chronicles of Darkness game where I was the ST. <hr /> It was just over a decade ago my sister died. I had just come home from serving a full time, 2 year long, religious mission. I had spent that time in deep meditation upon the word of god, sharing what I had learned and what I felt to be true, and speaking from the death of my soul and heart with anyone who would listen to me. I had trouble adjusting back to life without the constant scripture study, prayer, and teaching. Because of that I had trouble finding work but I was determined to find something because I was out I wasn't around when it happened. I don't know much about what happened, but what I do know is it was bloody, it was messy, and what ever did this it wasn't human, it wasn't natural. I'm not saying that to be dramatic, the thing that did this exerted such a sense of over kill that it obliterated her reducing her to a state that was without a doubt impossible under all normal conditions. Animals couldn't have done this, and a human...well even a suicide bombing wouldn't have left a mess like that. The police here in South East Wisconsin? Ha! They hadn't seen anything like this...ever.<br /> <br /> Motivated by my sister's death I threw myself into studying, religion in particular, but not my own. I had to dig deep into other religions, study what they knew because somewhere out there was a clue to the identity of what killed my sister. Sure I could have hung out with the ghost hunting club at UW but those people were amateurs playing with things they didn't understand, ignoring truths because they didn't want to accept the sources. The world's faiths in the purest forms tell us of things lurking in the darkness that most people now just assume were allegory rather than warnings of true monsters in the dark.<br /> <br /> I couldn't focus on christianity either, that would be rather pointless, all the cultural reforms it's been under likely buried a lot of truth. I couldn't keep going to UW, I needed a school that offered studies in the divine. I needed to dig deeper I needed to understand the threads I was studying on my own, in my own time. So many things were coming together. Scared paintings from the Navajo looking like sacred Buddhist paintings, both used for the same sort of rituals of blessing. That shouldn't be possible. Yeah sure minor differences but those differences looked to be the differences were in decorations not the important symbols. Not the Keys. What started as a search for answers to my sisters death turned into a bigger thing. Every moment I spent in study I found new threads linking things together that shouldn't be connected.<br /> <br /> I pulled and I dug at it, working like a man with a fever attending a predominate catholic university. You may have heard of Marquette University I graduated there with a degree in Theology probably their first mormon to do so and on a fencing scholarship. Shortly there after while researching a connection I found between threads in the book of mormon, an old hindu text, and an ancient buddhist scroll it hit me, I could see the connections, the symbols, hidden in the failures of understanding of the authors who just couldn't comprehend what they were seeing. It all made perfect sense! I looked up from my books and reflexively stood up my chair clattering to the floor.<br /> <br /> I wasn't in the library. I wasn't anywhere I recognized. Over head strange celestial beings moved on beautiful wings some both achingly beautiful and frightening in the same breath. I saw int he distance a great tower that seemed to be calling to me. I had to get there, I had to go to it. I started walking in that direction when I heard a voice say, &quot;Greetings traveler, be not afraid, I am Lashaelmuel, as the tower calls to the, thine soul called me. I turned to look upon beautiful woman with angelic wings. She was radiant to behold. I nearly fell back in a mix of divine awe struck fear, and being taken aback by such a beautiful woman. She looked at me and I swear she smiled. &quot;Come, I am your guide.&quot; She out stretched her hand to me and I took it, she had a good hand shake. She lead me though the world Aether I found it was called, a part of our world separated from the world I knew. Not be divine decree though but by the wickedness of very powerful men. I always said that God doesn't make junk, but men make junk out of what God has made. Turns out that was more the case than I thought. As she shared knowledge with me I was tested. My character put on trial in order to reach the tower. Other Seraphs and a few Cherubim helped with the testing. Probing questions about right and wrong, to which there seemed no wrong answer but to not reflect upon my own answer. That is until on the way to my final test I saw a woman being attacked by a beast. It didn't look like anything I had seen so far. I doubted this was a test. I moved forward and Lashaelmuel called out. &quot;If thou leaveth the path thine soul is in danger!&quot; She was afraid. I could not help it though I had to act. I grabbed up a rock from the ground and hurled it at the beast. I wanted to hurt it just enough to get it's attention away from the woman in danger. I had no time to think about what was happening. Just reach, throw, and go.<br /> <br /> I got the beasts attention and ended up being chased by it, it gave up on it's previous victim who was being much more difficult for an easier soul to devour, i.e. mine. I ran, as I did picking up rocks and throwing them with everything I had at the beast. These now that I can look back at it might have been my first spells. The beast chased me, hoping to consume me. Until eventually it shattered on the impact of one of the stones. Perhaps this beast, looking back, was an invasive spirit that found it's way into the Aether from the Abyss or another supernal realm. I'm not sure. What happened next amazed me. Lashaelmuel, was helping the other woman walk as she came over to me she looked bloody, and battered. She looked at me and then away and presented me with her sword. &quot;Here, your brave deed earned a reward, take this sword as your reward.&quot; She was speaking formally.<br /> &quot;I cannot, for this gift is far greater than any reward for any deed I have done here today.&quot; I said honestly refusing the gift. I didn't do what I did with thought of reward. I did it because it was the right thing to do.<br /> She looked a mix of shocked and offended. &quot;Take the sword, it is yours for risking your life to save mine, plus accept another gift of me if this is not worthy of your great deed.&quot; She sounded upset.<br /> &quot;I cannot this gift is now even greater, I did not act with thought of reward, please, this is too much.&quot; I said trying to reject the offer. I didn't want anything from her, why did she insist so. I heard Lashaelmuel giggle and she came over and whispered in my ear. &quot;No matter what she offers next time thou must accept it or thine refusal will deeply and irrevocably dishonor her.&quot;<br /> &quot;Accept this blade, a gift of me, and a gift of knowledge.&quot; She was almost growling. I think offering these things hurt her. I decided to accept like Lashaelmuel suggested.<br /> &quot;Your offer, I accept.&quot; I said defeated. I had to do this, I had to make sure that I didn't hurt her pride more, but that I also make sure the things I accepted were of little value. &quot;The knowledge I would ask is What is your name? and the gift is, a hug.&quot; There we go. Nothing offensive. Her eyes went livid when I mentioned her name though. When she processed the second part she looked at me.<br /> &quot;Why doest thou ask these things?&quot; She said confused. &quot;The name would grant thee power and I understand that, but the hug is a mere fleeting instant that can be a greeting, a farewell, or many things that are far from what I expected you to ask.&quot;<br /> &quot;Because I cannot use the power of that name, so it merely because the identity of the personage I met on my travel. The hug, because I felt it wouldn't hold much value to you, so you could give it away without it meaning much. The sword I felt was already too much. A blade crafted by angels, for angels, it...&quot; She held up her hand.<br /> &quot;A blade crafted for a summoned Seraph, to bind her, by a mortal mage. That blade is my least favorite, and I own many, most are far more significant than that.&quot; She handed over the blade. &quot;I am Sundrushael.&quot; She said leaning in and giving me a hug. &quot;I greet thee, traveler to the mage's tower, and thank you for your aid.&quot; When I looked down I realized the sword was belted to my waist. When had that happened?<br /> I bowed deeply to her. &quot;It was my pleasure, to have met you in the first place Sundrushael.&quot; I felt the tower tugging on me pulling me. Was I close to it? I looked around and was shocked at how close it was, it wasn't that close before I was practically at the door step.<br /> &quot;It seems, the tower believes your testing is over the measure of your soul completed and it is ready for you.&quot; Lashaelmuel walked to lead me away. &quot;come sister, bare witness to this mage's birth into magic.&quot; I followed the two Seraph as they walked with me it wasn't far at all, I looked to the left and to the right as I entered the tower. All around me were names, etched, carved penned, written into the tower. They stopped when we came to a blank space. Lashaelmuel looked upon me. &quot;You know what you must do next. But before you do, what have you learned on your journey.&quot;<br /> I spoke, it was many truths profound, personal, and of a nature that I cannot record them here. There are not words that are true enough in all the tongues of men to record what I need to write and I hope one day to be able to express them. As my heart poured out I cried, I embraced my guide, and my friends, I thanked them from every fiber of my being. My heart had burst in joy, in understanding, and I will never forget my journey and what I learned that day. I awoke in the hospital, the sword by me but the nurses didn't notice. I walked out of there with it upon my hip and no one noticed it. I rode the bus home, and no one noticed. I noticed though I could see the power in the blade, see the power and truth at the core of things. Hidden just below the surface. I joined the Arrows. I needed their guidance, and I needed to do something with my gift to better my fellow man and that meant conflict, and struggling. There is more than just a lie holding down the world. The lie is just a part of it. I have this gift not to just combat a lie, but to help others.<br /> <br /> While with in the training of the arrow I took the shadow name, Ammon after Ammon the Great Servant or Ammon the Missionary. I seemed to feel a sort of resonance with him, and his selfless, service. Though for the life of me I can't remember community service always seeming to involve this many gang members, thieves, and danger... Though I have to say I seem to remember being told to be careful in choosing my shadow name because it can have an influence on your life...this is just coincidence. Right? I teacher starting off was Sentinel John McCabe, also of the Orbromos Path. Nice guy, but once he felt I understood enough to handle myself he kicked me out into the real world and said not to contact him until I was ready for the next step, the really hard stuff. It was during my training that I realized after all our checking and searching that my bonded tool was a swiss army knife I had been carrying in my pocket. I was a boyscout and had carried one in my pocket every place I could. It wasn't so much a weapon as a universal tool. If there is a situation you can be in that a Swiss Army knife can't help you get out of, it's because death is there waiting for you and he'll be damned before he lets the a pocket knife get the better of him again.<br /> <br /> In the present day though, my dreams became troubled. My dead sister speaks to me, shows me visions of fleeting friends, forgotten, people I used to know changed by the darkness, herself changed. She is giving me a warning. A danger is coming, a storm on the horizon, an assassin. It's coming for me. For these who could have been my friends. I don't know what or who this storm is, but...my dream told me a specific day and time to be at a certain place. I'm not missing that meeting. <hr /><br /> <b>Shadow Name:</b> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ammon_(Book_of_Mormon_missionary)\" target=\"_blank\">Ammon</a><br /> <b>Concept:</b> So none have to go through my pain<br /> <b>Path:</b> Obromos<br /> <b>Player:</b> Me!<br /> <b>Virtue:</b> Loyalty<br /> <b>Order:</b> Adamant Arrow<br /> <b>Chronicle:</b> Yet Unnamed<br /> <b>Vice:</b> Addictive<br /> <b>Legacy:</b> None yet chosen <div align=\"center\"><b><span style=\"font-size:14px\">Attributes</span></b></div> <div align=\"center\">Int: 3 Str: 2 Pres: 3<br /> Wit: 1 Dex: 2 Mani: 2<br /> Res: 4 Stam: 2 Comp: 3</div> <div align=\"center\"><b>Skills</b> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table align=\"center\" class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"width: 500px; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Mental</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Physical</b></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"><b>Social</b></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Academics (Religon) 3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Athletics (Aim Spell) 2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Empathy 1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Computer 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Brawl 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Expression 1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Crafts 2</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Firearms 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Intimidation 1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Investigation 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Weapony (blades) 3</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Persuion 1</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Occult 4</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\">Science 1</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 1px; padding: 1px\"></td> </tr> </table></div> </div> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Arcana</b><br /> Forces 2, Matter 1, Prime 3<br /> <br /> <b>Merits: </b><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1bskhz4dD92xcSlcYWB5fySitcziJoVOR-nG6AHusPB8/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Enhanced Item</a> 5<br /> Hallow 1<br /> Resources 1<br /> Shadow Name 2<br /> <br /> <b>Health:</b> 7<br /> <b>Will:</b> 7<br /> <b>Size:</b> 5<br /> <b>Speed:</b> 9<br /> <b>Gnosis:</b> 1<br /> <b>Dedicated Tool:</b> Swiss Army Knife<br /> <b>Paraxis:</b> Control Gravity<br /> Nimbus:<br /> Long: Scriptures open to exactly the page someone needs to read. Immediate: A tree with fruit of purest white. Tilt: ?<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations</b><br /> Protect the Sisters (nuns), and women, at the Metcalfe Park Women's Sanctuary from the gangs.<br /> Defeat a Supernatural being with Suraphiel<br /> Find and bring to justice my sister's killer.<br /> <br /> <b>Obsessions</b><br /> Discover magics connection to the Divine.<br /> <br /> <b>Rotes:</b><br /> Forces 2 Invisibility science<br /> Prime 3 Aetheric Winds Athletics<br /> Matter 1 Craftsman eye Crafts<br /> <br /> Weapons Suraphiel, and light pistol.<br /> Armor: Kevlar Vest","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":600,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","user":"HaplessWithDice","date":". 09-10-2016, 08:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:09:21-07:00","id":966192,"title":"","content":"Realized I left out my obsession, Aspirations, and how I choose my Shadow Name....Editing to add these details now.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:20:54-07:00","id":966198,"title":"","content":"So, reading the backstory, why did he decide religion had an answer? You don't give an explanation you just act like it's obvious, but he could have just as easily started cruising with ghost hunters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:36:17-07:00","id":966205,"title":"","content":"Asperations should really be something concrete. The first and second should probably be reworked with more objective Aspirations that can help drive action and be actively worked towards. The second in particular is kind of useless for both you and the ST.<br /> <br /> And no, you don't have to pick a legacy now. In fact, you really can't pick a legacy until Gnosis 2 at a minimum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:42:40-07:00","id":966210,"title":"","content":"What does addictive legacy mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:50:02-07:00","id":966218,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> His Vice is Addictive. It's just hard to read.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1090276-2e-moinen-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\">[2E] Moinen's Homebrew Hub</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1747-moinen","name":"Moinen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1747_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"889"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:50:32-07:00","id":966219,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right?p=966198#post966198\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, reading the backstory, why did he decide religion had an answer? You don't give an explanation you just act like it's obvious, but he could have just as easily started cruising with ghost hunters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess to me it's obvious but I'll go back and try to adjust that. Explain the logic.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right?p=966205#post966205\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Asperations should really be something concrete. The first and second should probably be reworked with more objective Aspirations that can help drive action and be actively worked towards. The second in particular is kind of useless for both you and the ST.<br /> <br /> And no, you don't have to pick a legacy now. In fact, you really can't pick a legacy until Gnosis 2 at a minimum.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Okay Adjusted the Aspirations. I think that's right. I altered the first to focus on the particular women's shelter, and the problem it faces.<br /> The second, I just figured that was something concrete and helps move to the long term one. Since I know something supernatural killed my sister, I have to be able to defeat a supernatural being of a lesser order before I go after this one.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T07:58:06-07:00","id":966223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right?p=966210#post966210\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What does addictive legacy mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's Vice Addictive, looks like the formatting is hard to read I'll adjust that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moinen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right?p=966218#post966218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2632\" data-vbnamecard=\"2632\">Mrmdubois</a> His Vice is Addictive. It's just hard to read.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll fix up the formatting Is that better?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:19:01-07:00","id":966233,"title":"","content":"Formatting fix works. Background still has me wondering how his sister dying motivated him to study religion, or hope that religion has a name for whatever killed his sister. You're probably working on that though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2632-mrmdubois","name":"Mrmdubois","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6827"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T08:46:24-07:00","id":966254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mrmdubois</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right?p=966233#post966233\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Formatting fix works. Background still has me wondering how his sister dying motivated him to study religion, or hope that religion has a name for whatever killed his sister. You're probably working on that though.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought I put that in. The idea that the worlds religions recorded many threats to humanity but most of those in the modern world are just though of as allegory, instead of being very real, and dangerous things. That and given the cultural logic that is the first thing he would do, turn to the divine for answers. It's just turning there for one answer he found other questions, other threads that were important on a level he could feel. Although hold on. Probably a cultural detail I over looked to add be back with something added in a second. Preview of it being.<br /> <br /> &quot;I had just gotten back from serving a 2 year full time religious mission, spending my days in prayer, preaching, and meditation upon the scriptures.&quot; That is going in the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:19:06-07:00","id":966268,"title":"","content":"Also, you can't have Celestial Fire as a Praxis, as you only have Prime 2.<br /> Edit: Well, you can, but having a spell you can't cast as a Praxis isn't the best move.<br /> Edit2: From what we know of the Errata, starting characters get 3 Rotes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4854-justin-sane","name":"Justin Sane","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T09:24:15-07:00","id":966270,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justin Sane</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966181-ammon-the-mage-did-i-do-this-right?p=966268#post966268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, you can't have Celestial Fire as a Praxis, as you only have Prime 2.<br /> Edit: Well, you can, but having a spell you can't cast as a Praxis isn't the best move.<br /> Edit2: From what we know of the Errata, starting characters get 3 Rotes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I haven't seen the Errata Well then no sense taking two prime rotes. Might as well take a prime two. I must have misunderstood how Praxis worked I figured I could cast the spell but for the purpose of Spell effects it counted as my current Arcana. Guess I'll adjust that as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T19:14:56-07:00","id":966534,"title":"","content":"i like the idea of character critique in this forum.....i like the backstory...ill get cracking on mine and post it as well.<br /> <br /> where is the errata sheet ???<br /> <br /> Raphael","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12391-rtemplar","name":"rtemplar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-09T20:13:56-07:00","id":966555,"title":"","content":"I have always found a bit of critique useful. It helps to flesh out things, after all what was clear in my mind was not clear to mrmdubious. So having more eyes really helps improve understanding. Like how I somehow thought that a mage could cast a Praxis spell that was from a higher dot level than their normal spells, just not getting the free reach and possibly needing to reach for every dot they didn't have. Not sure why I thought that. Must have been temporary insanity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T08:08:44-07:00","id":967316,"title":"","content":"Reading the fluff the sword makes more sence as an Artifact, IMHO","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow?p=925424#post925424\" target=\"_blank\">Simurgh</a>, Mysterium Thyrsus in Mountains of Shadow (<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/939031-ic-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">IC</a>|<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/play-by-post/924216-ooc-mage-the-awakening-2e-mountains-of-shadow\" target=\"_blank\">OOC</a>)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov","name":"Tambov","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6508_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"455"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-09-11T11:17:50-07:00","id":967415,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6508-tambov\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar6508_3.jpg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"6508\" data-vbnamecard=\"6508\">Tambov</a> Well the sword was made by a human, for a seraph (probably to bind her but I left that vague on purpose) but I could see it working as a artifact in every way but mechanically. Mechanically it is supposed to grant one or two passive bonuses as always on effects that are properties put into the object. Which is why I went with enhanced object because that is the definition of enhanced object.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-10-02T18:55:55-07:00","id":980512,"title":"","content":"Hello. I figured I'd give an update on how things are going.<br /> <br /> First. Ammon didn't happen. ST scrapped him. Thanks for all the work, but we worked out a new concept. Allow me to introduce <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1Owye-BubAK2xl-udv8ylClwcV2GPBNJE4E9YghErNJA/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Ma'ii</a><br /> <br /> Ma'ii is darker mage, same person as Ammon but because his sister's death wasn't so close after spending all those years as a missionary and having been through so many failures himself, he fit more the Moros path. Ma'ii is still a bit upset and wants to push and challenge the boundaries constantly which is why his status in the arrow has never improved.<br /> <br /> I had this idea that when he acts under the purview of his shadow name he puts on a black coyote mask with red around the eyes. This idea comes from the depiction I heard of the Navajo Coyote as being black in color with eyes made of balls of burning pine pitch. Is doing this thing with the Mask a good idea to help create a separation between his shadow identity and his mundane identity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}